import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a6 as o}from"./chunks/framework.B8j4beN0.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Build with Feluqa","description":"Create applications with Feluqa, understand product rights, and work with the NUMERIMONDES team.","frontmatter":{"sidebarTitle":"License","icon":"scale","title":"Build with Feluqa","description":"Create applications with Feluqa, understand product rights, and work with the NUMERIMONDES team.","summary":"Explains that building Applications for personal, commercial, organizational, and authorized client work is free of charge and that creators may use the Products they create. It distinguishes the proprietary developer kit (SDK) and Platform from customer Products, describes contribution and selective open-source direction, provides company legal information, and outlines product-development options.","date":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z","lastmod":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z","weight":2,"status":"Exploring","tags":["feluqa","licence","proprietary","contributors"],"draft":true,"author":{"name":"El Moumen Yassine","url":"https://numerimondes.com","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/elmoumenyassine","email":"yassine@numerimondes.com"}},"headers":[],"relativePath":"prologue/licence.md","filePath":"prologue/licence.md"}'),r={name:"prologue/licence.md"};function n(s,e,l,d,c,u){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="build-with-feluqa" tabindex="-1">Build with Feluqa <a class="header-anchor" href="#build-with-feluqa" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Build with Feluqa&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Creating an <strong>Application</strong> with Feluqa&#39;s developer tools (the software development kit, or SDK) is free of charge for personal projects and commercial work. Individuals and organisations can build Applications with it; contractors and subcontractors can build them for clients when authorised to do so. You are free to use the <strong>Products</strong> you create for yourself, your organisation, or your client. This right to use your Products is guaranteed.</p><h2 id="feluqa-platform-and-licensing" tabindex="-1">Feluqa Platform and licensing <a class="header-anchor" href="#feluqa-platform-and-licensing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Feluqa Platform and licensing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Feluqa SDK</strong> is the development API and tools used to create Applications. Its use for Application creation is free of charge. The shared runtime and administration services (the <strong>Feluqa Platform</strong>) provide capabilities such as identity, access control, audit, and configuration; the Platform is distinct from a customer&#39;s Product.</p><p>Both the SDK and Platform are proprietary software owned by NUMERIMONDES SARL AU. Proprietary describes ownership; it does not take away your guaranteed right to create Applications and use the Products built with them, or your right to contribute to Feluqa and help others build with it through the collaboration process.</p><p>The applicable terms distinguish rights to Feluqa&#39;s SDK and Platform components from rights in a Product, its Applications and Modules, and customer-specific source code. These terms use Feluqa&#39;s <a href="/get-started/introduction/taxonomy">canonical taxonomy</a>.</p><p>Feluqa currently has one SDK. Additional SDKs may be developed for different audiences or application profiles.</p><p>Some Feluqa software components (Rust crates) will be released under open-source licences over time. Each release will identify the components, licence, and applicable versions. Other components may remain unpublished to meet the security, operational, contractual, or strategic needs of civilian, research, military, and government deployments. This can apply even when a component contains no client-specific business logic or deployment configuration. These decisions are made component by component; keeping source private is not, by itself, a security guarantee.</p><p>Employees, subcontractors, and AI agents may work within the rights granted to their organisation. Third-party components remain subject to their own licences and notices.</p><p>For full copyright and licence information, consult the licence materials distributed with the relevant source code or the Licences resource in the System Control Panel, when available.</p><h2 id="why-feluqa-is-proprietary" tabindex="-1">Why Feluqa is proprietary <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-feluqa-is-proprietary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Why Feluqa is proprietary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Proprietary software is not inherently good or bad; it is an ownership and distribution model. For Feluqa, it lets NUMERIMONDES steward an integrated platform and sustain work across SDKs, runtimes, development tools, deployment, and operations. Application creation remains free, and organisations can build with their own engineers. The product strategy is to provide systemic breadth in the platform while letting users and their agents provide domain depth through their own Modules.</p><p>The commercial ambition is to build a durable, differentiated position in military software and software for small and medium-sized enterprises. Proprietary technology is part of that strategy: the goal is to create a distinct product that is difficult to substitute and sustain it as a business. This is an ambition, not a claim that Feluqa has already achieved a tenfold technical advantage or market leadership.</p><p>We believe that lasting companies build differentiated technology and serve markets where they can establish a defensible position. Feluqa&#39;s own thesis adds that modern development tools make broad platform capabilities more attainable for a small team, while users and their agents can shape the specialized business workflows. We describe this as <a href="/agents/agentic-development/agent-ready-extensible-modules">“breadth is now affordable, depth belongs to users”</a>.</p><p>Proprietary ownership does not by itself prove that software is safer, more reliable, or technically superior. Those qualities require implementation, evidence, and review. The ownership model describes who controls Feluqa and what rights are granted; it does not replace security, operational, or contractual commitments.</p><h2 id="contributions" tabindex="-1">Contributions <a class="header-anchor" href="#contributions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contributions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>We welcome contributions and want to work closely with the people who make them. Contact Feluqa through <a href="https://github.com/feluqa/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a> to discuss your idea. Maintainers will work with you on scope, access, and contribution terms before work is incorporated. See the <a href="/prologue/contribution-guide">Contribution Guide</a> for how to get started and <a href="/feluqa-internals/">Core Contribution</a> for engineering guidance. The Feluqa Platform remains proprietary; agreed terms make clear how your contribution may be used in proprietary or open-source components.</p><h2 id="legal-overview" tabindex="-1">Legal Overview <a class="header-anchor" href="#legal-overview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Legal Overview&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Official identifiers, registered purpose, and company documents for Numerimondes SARL AU.</p><h3 id="legal-identity" tabindex="-1">Legal Identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#legal-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Legal Identity&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Registered name</strong></td><td>Numerimondes SARL AU</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Legal form</strong></td><td>SARL AU (single-shareholder limited company)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Patente</strong></td><td>Conseil en gestion (management consulting)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Headquarters</strong></td><td>10 Rue de la Liberté, 3rd floor, apt. 5, Casablanca</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Founder &amp; Manager</strong></td><td>Yassine El Moumen</td></tr><tr><td><strong>RC</strong></td><td>152844</td></tr><tr><td><strong>ICE</strong></td><td>003396233000077</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Email</strong></td><td><a href="mailto:contact@numerimondes.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">contact@numerimondes.com</a></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Phone</strong></td><td>+212 6 20 99 06 92</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="registered-purpose-objet-social" tabindex="-1">Registered Purpose (<em>Objet Social</em>) <a class="header-anchor" href="#registered-purpose-objet-social" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Registered Purpose (*Objet Social*)&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The text below is taken verbatim from the company&#39;s statutes (<em>statuts de la société</em>). It is the legal purpose registered with Moroccan authorities—not a marketing summary.</p><p>Day-to-day positioning and services are available on <a href="https://numerimondes.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">numerimondes.com</a>.</p><p><strong>Patente:</strong> management consulting.</p><p>The Company has for its purpose, in Morocco and abroad, for its own account as well as for the account of third parties:</p><ul><li>Commercial development consulting;</li><li>Information systems consulting and software development;</li><li>Information technology consulting and digital transformation;</li><li>Digital marketing consulting;</li><li>Consulting, control, and audit in security, safety, and cybersecurity;</li><li>E-learning and training; organisation of turnkey seminars, conferences, and modular training programmes; in-company training and pedagogical engineering;</li><li>Management and operation of telephone contact centres;</li><li>Recruitment, human-resources strategy consulting, career development, and skills evaluation;</li><li>Representation and exploitation of all patents, trademarks, or licences for IT and industrial products, accessories, and solutions;</li><li>Purchase, import, sale, and export of all IT equipment and materials; management, installation, fit-out, and operation of any commercial or industrial unit suited to the activities listed above.</li></ul><p>And more generally, all commercial, industrial, financial, movable, and real-estate operations related directly or indirectly to the above purposes, or likely to favour their achievement and development.</p><h2 id="want-a-product-built-with-feluqa" tabindex="-1">Want a Product Built with Feluqa? <a class="header-anchor" href="#want-a-product-built-with-feluqa" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Want a Product Built with Feluqa?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>NUMERIMONDES works with organisations that want a Product created with Feluqa. Start a conversation about the users, workflows, operating environment, and delivery goals. A written proposal will define the scope, deliverables, rights in customer-specific work, Feluqa usage rights, deployment, support, maintenance, and any fees before work begins. Commercial terms may include development, licensing, support, or maintenance fees; terms are agreed for each engagement.</p><h3 id="build-with-your-own-team" tabindex="-1">Build with your own team <a class="header-anchor" href="#build-with-your-own-team" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Build with your own team&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Organisations can have their own engineers build and maintain Products with Feluqa. NUMERIMONDES can discuss the required access, usage rights, onboarding, and support. A client&#39;s engineers may propose improvements to the Feluqa SDK; changes are reviewed against the development guidelines, product architecture, and security requirements, and contribution terms are agreed before accepted work is incorporated.</p><h3 id="find-people-to-build-with-feluqa" tabindex="-1">Find people to build with Feluqa <a class="header-anchor" href="#find-people-to-build-with-feluqa" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Find people to build with Feluqa&quot;">​</a></h3><p>NUMERIMONDES can use its in-house recruitment activity to help identify and assemble a qualified team for a Feluqa project. A directory of people with Feluqa experience is planned; profiles will be published only with each person&#39;s agreement and with their experience clearly described.</p>',34)])])}const m=t(r,[["render",n]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
